meta {
  name: List OPD Master Data
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/opd-master-data?page=1&limit=20
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 20
  ~search: main
  ~branchId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data.length && data[0].id) bru.setEnvVar("opdMasterDataId", data[0].id);
}

docs {
  OPD equivalent of the lab **List Master Data** endpoint (GET /opd-master-data).
  
  Paginated list of the tenant's master data. `page`/`limit` optional. Captures
  `opdMasterDataId` from the first item — the easiest way to grab the master data
  that was **auto-created** when a branch was created.

  Every branch gets a default master data automatically on branch creation (named
  after the branch), so this list is populated as soon as you have branches. Also
  feeds the "copy data from" dropdown on **Create Master Data**.

  ## Filters (all optional — toggle the `~` to enable a query param)

  - `search` — case-insensitive `contains` match on `name`.
  - `branchId` — only master data belonging to that branch (UUID). Read filter
    only; tenant scoping + RLS already guard cross-tenant access.
}
